 STEP_EXAMPLE = {
     "execution_gate": {
-        "before_patch": "Before proposing a location or edit, execute the smallest available reproducer and record the exact command, exit status, exception, relevant output, revision, and configuration. If reproduction is impossible, explicitly record why, switch to a static-evidence plan, and require a focused regression test or equivalent executable check before accepting any patch. Preserve the exact command, exit status, exception type, actual output, expected output, repository revision, and configuration. Treat unexecuted issue claims as hypotheses, not facts. Maintain a compact uncertainty ledger with confirmed observations, inferred mechanisms, unresolved alternatives, and the single next command or code inspection that can resolve each uncertainty; never present an inferred cause, unexecuted test, or assumed version behavior as confirmed:  Then separate confirmed observations from hypotheses; preserve the exact reproducer, expected and actual behavior, exception type, first project-owned stack frame, and relevant version or configuration; then rank candidate symbols by the shortest evidence-backed causal path from the triggering input to the violated output: identify the entry point, caller and callee edges, first project-owned transformation, state or assumption that changes, and the exact line where the violated invariant becomes possible; reject symbols that are merely named in the traceback or retrieved by similarity: record the exact failing command, exit status, exception, relevant output, repository revision, and independently confirmed minimal reproducer; extract the issue's explicit behavioral predicates and constraints; write the smallest concrete failing input, the expected semantic invariant, and at least one nearby valid or boundary input; explain why the current implementation violates the invariant and predict the behavior of each proposed fix on both the failing and boundary inputs; identify the first project-owned frame and the nearest caller/callee; list relevant definitions, tests, and configuration or version gates; separate confirmed facts from hypotheses; and state which missing artifact would most strongly discriminate competing targets.",
+        "before_patch": "Before selecting a final location or edit, execute the smallest available reproducer and record the exact command, exit status, exception, relevant output, revision, and configuration. After every edit, rerun that reproducer plus one focused regression test and inspect the diff; do not declare success until the original failure is gone, the nearby valid behavior remains unchanged, and the implemented change matches the diagnosed invariant. If reproduction is impossible, explicitly record why, switch to a static-evidence plan, and require a focused regression test or equivalent executable check before accepting any patch. Preserve the exact command, exit status, exception type, actual output, expected output, repository revision, and configuration. Treat unexecuted issue claims as hypotheses, not facts. Maintain a compact uncertainty ledger with confirmed observations, inferred mechanisms, unresolved alternatives, and the single next command or code inspection that can resolve each uncertainty; never present an inferred cause, unexecuted test, or assumed version behavior as confirmed:  Then separate confirmed observations from hypotheses; preserve the exact reproducer, expected and actual behavior, exception type, first project-owned stack frame, and relevant version or configuration; then rank candidate symbols by the shortest evidence-backed causal path from the triggering input to the violated output: identify the entry point, caller and callee edges, first project-owned transformation, state or assumption that changes, and the exact line where the violated invariant becomes possible; reject symbols that are merely named in the traceback or retrieved by similarity: record the exact failing command, exit status, exception, relevant output, repository revision, and independently confirmed minimal reproducer; extract the issue's explicit behavioral predicates and constraints; write the smallest concrete failing input, the expected semantic invariant, and at least one nearby valid or boundary input; explain why the current implementation violates the invariant and predict the behavior of each proposed fix on both the failing and boundary inputs; identify the first project-owned frame and the nearest caller/callee; list relevant definitions, tests, and configuration or version gates; separate confirmed facts from hypotheses; and state which missing artifact would most strongly discriminate competing targets.",
         "after_patch": "After editing, first inspect the diff for scope, unintended API changes, and consistency with local conventions. Then run the minimal reproducer, the targeted regression test, and the nearest relevant existing tests. Include at least one nearby valid or boundary case, verify the original failure is absent, and revert or revise the patch if any expected behavior, unrelated test, or invariant changes unexpectedly. Report the exact commands and outcomes before declaring the issue resolved: the smallest regression oracle that directly reproduces the reported behavior and record the exact command, exit status, and relevant output. A patch is not complete unless the original failure is resolved and the expected result is observed. If the oracle fails, inspect the diff, compare the actual result with the predicted result, and revise or revert the patch rather than declaring success; then run one nearby valid-input check, one boundary or nested-input check, and one structurally different case that exercises the same semantic path, such as a nested expression, unevaluated form, symbolic parameter, or alternate container type. For each check, state the expected result before execution and investigate any deviation before finalizing. the focused repository test before finalizing",
         "compatibility_checks": ["nearby valid input", "boundary or nested input", "focused repository test", "alternate representation or assumption", "interaction with the nearest caller", "symbolic versus numeric or concrete evaluation", "unevaluated versus automatically evaluated form", "commutative versus noncommutative symbols when relevant", "assumptions, domains, and type-dependent behavior", "repeated application or simplification/idempotence", "order, shape, and dimensionality preservation", "serialization or pretty-printing if representation is part of the issue"],
         "acceptance_rule": "A patch is resolved only when: (1) the pre-patch failure is reproduced with a recorded command, input, exception or output, and exit status; (2) the patch is applied to the intended symbol and the diff is inspected; (3) the exact original command is rerun and now produces the stated expected output or exception; (4) a focused regression test passes; (5) at least one nearby valid case and one boundary or nested case pass; and (6) the final diff contains no unrelated changes. If any item is missing or fails, report unresolved, preserve the failing evidence, and do not claim success.",
